                <pb facs="0171" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1950v02/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.357/10–2050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Snow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   niact </hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Oslo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-10-20T16:00:00+01:00">October 20, 1950—4
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>405. Reference Deptel 288, October 19. Saw Foreign Minister<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d82-f1"/> this noon. He said Norwegian UN delegate had sought
                    instructions and he had replied directing vote against Indian proposal. He
                    stated these instructions unequivocal permitting delegation no alternatives and
                    that he was gratified learn that US was maintaining its stand favor of Lie’s
                    continuance in office. He asked whether I knew what British position would be. I
                    replied had no knowledge, but imagined if prominent Commonwealth candidate put
                    forward, might slightly complicate British viewpoint. He said British UN
                    delegate told him very recently British not interested seeing Indian as
                    Secretary General.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Snow</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
